# MCP Client Unified Architecture Plan

## Executive Summary

**Goal:** Eliminate type duplication between our code and pmcp by using pmcp types directly, complete TODO implementations

**Why Now:** We just integrated pmcp for both server and client. Time to fully leverage it and complete incomplete features.

**Breaking Changes:** Yes, but we're pre-1.0 and this is the right time. Deprecated aliases provide migration path.

**Time Estimate:** Careful, methodical implementation - Phase 1 this session

**Result:** Single unified type system, validated schemas, structured content, complete implementations

---

## Current State Analysis

### Architecture Overview

```
botticelli_mcp/           # Server-side MCP (tools/resources)
├── pmcp_server.rs        # Uses pmcp::Server ✅
├── pmcp_adapters.rs      # Adapts our tools to pmcp ✅
├── pmcp_middleware.rs    # Observability middleware ✅
└── tools/                # Our MCP tool implementations ✅

botticelli_mcp_client/    # Client-side MCP (connecting to servers)
├── external_client.rs    # Uses pmcp::Client ✅ (COMPLETE)
├── client.rs             # Internal orchestration ⚠️ (INCOMPLETE)
├── tool_executor.rs      # Tool execution ⚠️ (STUBBED)
├── schema/               # Provider-specific conversions ⚠️
└── llm_adapter.rs        # LLM integration ⚠️ (INCOMPLETE)
```

### Type Duplication Issues

**Problem 1: ToolDefinition Duplication**

```rust
// botticelli_mcp_client/src/tool_executor.rs (OUR CUSTOM TYPE)
pub struct ToolDefinition {
    pub name: String,
    pub description: String,
    pub input_schema: Value,  // Unvalidated JSON
}

// pmcp exports (from docs.rs/pmcp)
pub struct Tool {
    pub name: String,
    pub description: Option<String>,
    pub input_schema: JsonSchema,  // Validated schema!
}
```

**Impact:**
- external_client.rs converts pmcp::Tool → our ToolDefinition (lines 191-199)
- Manual conversions everywhere
- Schema inconsistencies (Value vs JsonSchema)
- No validation leverage from pmcp
- Maintenance burden on two type systems

**Problem 2: Unstructured Results**

```rust
// Current: tool results are raw JSON Value
pub async fn execute(&self, tool_name: &str, arguments: Value) -> McpClientResult<Value> {
    // ⚠️ No structure, no type safety
    Ok(json!({"status": "success"}))
}

// pmcp provides: Structured Content types
pub enum Content {
    Text(TextContent),
    Image(ImageContent),
    Resource(ResourceContent),
}
```

**Impact:**
- Lose semantic meaning of results
- Can't distinguish text from images from resources
- Manual parsing everywhere downstream
- No type-safe access to content

**Problem 3: Incomplete Implementations (TODOs)**

```rust
// tool_executor.rs:38-49
pub async fn execute(&self, tool_name: &str, _arguments: Value) -> McpClientResult<Value> {
    // TODO: Actual tool execution will integrate with MCP server
    // ⚠️ Returns placeholder!
    Ok(json!({"status": "success", "tool": tool_name}))
}
```

**Found in:**
- `tool_executor.rs` - Tool execution stubbed
- `client.rs` - Needs audit
- `llm_adapter.rs` - Needs audit
- `context.rs` - Needs audit

