### Step 1.3: Structured Content Types

**Objective:** Use pmcp::types::Content for tool results instead of raw Value

**Current State:**
```rust
// tool_executor.rs
pub async fn execute(&self, tool_name: &str, arguments: Value) -> McpClientResult<Value> {
    // Returns unstructured JSON - loses semantic meaning
}

// external_client.rs:276-281
serde_json::to_value(result.content).map_err(|e| {
    // Converts structured Content back to unstructured Value!
})
```

**Target State:**
```rust
use pmcp::types::{Content, TextContent, ImageContent, ResourceContent};

pub async fn execute(&self, tool_name: &str, arguments: Value) 
    -> McpClientResult<Vec<Content>> {
    // Returns structured, type-safe content
}

pub async fn call_tool(&mut self, tool_name: &str, arguments: Value) 
    -> McpClientResult<Vec<Content>> {
    // Returns pmcp Content directly - no conversion!
}
```

**Tasks:**

1. **Update external_client.rs call_tool:**
   ```rust
   // OLD (lines 276-281) - throws away structure
   serde_json::to_value(result.content).map_err(|e| {
       McpClientError::new(McpClientErrorKind::SerializationError(
           format!("Failed to serialize tool result: {}", e)
       ))
   })
   
   // NEW - return Content directly, preserve structure
   Ok(result.content)
   ```

2. **Update tool_executor.rs:**
   ```rust
   use pmcp::types::{Content, TextContent};
   
   pub struct ToolExecutor {
       tools: HashMap<String, Tool>,
   }
   
   impl ToolExecutor {
       pub async fn execute(&self, tool_name: &str, arguments: Value) 
           -> McpClientResult<Vec<Content>> {
           
           let tool = self.tools.get(tool_name)
               .ok_or_else(|| McpClientError::new(
                   McpClientErrorKind::ToolNotFound(tool_name.to_string())
               ))?;
           
           // TODO: Implement actual tool execution (Phase 2)
           // For now, return structured text content
           Ok(vec![Content::Text(TextContent {
               text: format!("Tool {} executed successfully", tool_name),
               annotations: None,
           })])
       }
   }
   ```

3. **Update return type everywhere:**
   ```rust
   // Update all signatures that return tool results:
   // - external_client.rs: call_tool
   // - tool_executor.rs: execute
   // - Any downstream consumers
   ```

4. **Add Content helper methods:**
   ```rust
   // Create new file: src/content_helpers.rs
   use pmcp::types::{Content, TextContent, ImageContent, ResourceContent};
   
   /// Extract text from Content vector
   pub fn extract_text(content: &[Content]) -> String {
       content.iter()
           .filter_map(|c| match c {
               Content::Text(t) => Some(t.text.clone()),
               _ => None,
           })
           .collect::<Vec<_>>()
           .join("\n")
   }
   
   /// Extract all resources from Content vector
   pub fn extract_resources(content: &[Content]) -> Vec<ResourceContent> {
       content.iter()
           .filter_map(|c| match c {
               Content::Resource(r) => Some(r.clone()),
               _ => None,
           })
           .collect()
   }
   
   /// Extract images from Content vector
   pub fn extract_images(content: &[Content]) -> Vec<ImageContent> {
       content.iter()
           .filter_map(|c| match c {
               Content::Image(img) => Some(img.clone()),
               _ => None,
           })
           .collect()
   }
   
   /// Check if content contains any errors
   pub fn has_errors(content: &[Content]) -> bool {
       content.iter().any(|c| matches!(c, Content::Error(_)))
   }
   ```

5. **Update error types:**
   ```rust
   // error.rs - add Content-related errors if needed
   #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, derive_more::Display)]
   pub enum McpClientErrorKind {
       // ... existing variants
       
       #[display("Invalid content type: expected {}, got {}", expected, actual)]
       InvalidContentType { expected: String, actual: String },
   }
   ```

6. **Update lib.rs exports:**
   ```rust
   // Export Content helper functions
   pub use content_helpers::{
       extract_text, extract_resources, extract_images, has_errors
   };
   
   // Re-export pmcp Content types for convenience
   pub use pmcp::types::{Content, TextContent, ImageContent, ResourceContent};
   ```

**Testing:**
```bash
just test-package botticelli_mcp_client
```

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- ✅ call_tool returns Vec<Content>
- ✅ execute returns Vec<Content>
- ✅ Content helper methods implemented and tested
- ✅ Tests updated for structured content
- ✅ Documentation examples updated
- ✅ Type safety improved (no raw JSON)

**Estimated Impact:**
- Files changed: 5-6
- Breaking: Yes (return type change)
- Risk: Medium (affects downstream consumers)
- Benefit: High (type safety, semantic preservation)

