## Phase 3: Integration Testing

**Status:** After Phase 1 & 2

**Goal:** Validate full external server integration with real MCP servers

### Step 3.1: Filesystem Server Integration Test

**Objective:** Real end-to-end test with @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem

**Prerequisites:**
- Node.js installed
- npm available
- Temp directory for testing

**Tasks:**

1. **Create integration test:**
   ```rust
   // tests/filesystem_integration_test.rs
   
   use botticelli_mcp_client::{
       ExternalMcpClient, ExternalServerConfig,
       extract_text, Content,
   };
   use serde_json::json;
   
   #[tokio::test]
   #[cfg_attr(not(feature = "integration"), ignore)]
   async fn test_filesystem_server_read_file() {
       // Create test file
       let test_dir = std::env::temp_dir();
       let test_file = test_dir.join("mcp_integration_test.txt");
       std::fs::write(&test_file, "Hello MCP Integration!").unwrap();
       
       // Spawn real MCP filesystem server
       let config = ExternalServerConfig::builder()
           .name("filesystem".to_string())
           .command("npx".to_string())
           .args(vec![
               "-y".to_string(),
               "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem".to_string(),
               test_dir.to_string_lossy().to_string(),
           ])
           .build();
       
       let mut client = ExternalMcpClient::connect(config)
           .await
           .expect("Failed to connect to filesystem server");
       
       // Verify tool discovery
       let tools = client.tools();
       assert!(
           tools.iter().any(|t| t.name == "read_file"),
           "filesystem server should have read_file tool"
       );
       
       // Call read_file tool
       let result: Vec<Content> = client.call_tool(
           "read_file",
           json!({ "path": test_file.to_string_lossy() })
       ).await.expect("Failed to read file");
       
       // Extract and verify text content
       let text = extract_text(&result);
       assert!(
           text.contains("Hello MCP Integration!"),
           "File content should match: got '{}'", text
       );
       
       // Cleanup
       std::fs::remove_file(test_file).ok();
   }
   
   #[tokio::test]
   #[cfg_attr(not(feature = "integration"), ignore)]
   async fn test_filesystem_server_list_directory() {
       let test_dir = std::env::temp_dir();
       
       let config = ExternalServerConfig::builder()
           .name("filesystem".to_string())
           .command("npx".to_string())
           .args(vec![
               "-y".to_string(),
               "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem".to_string(),
               test_dir.to_string_lossy().to_string(),
           ])
           .build();
       
       let mut client = ExternalMcpClient::connect(config).await.unwrap();
       
       // List directory
       let result: Vec<Content> = client.call_tool(
           "list_directory",
           json!({ "path": test_dir.to_string_lossy() })
       ).await.expect("Failed to list directory");
       
       let text = extract_text(&result);
       assert!(!text.is_empty(), "Directory listing should not be empty");
   }
   ```

2. **Add feature flag:**
   ```toml
   # Cargo.toml
   [features]
   default = []
   integration = []  # For integration tests requiring external tools
   ```

3. **Add justfile recipe:**
   ```makefile
   # justfile
   
   # Run integration tests (requires Node.js/npm)
   test-integration:
       cargo test --package botticelli_mcp_client \
                  --features integration \
                  -- --include-ignored
   ```

4. **Document integration testing:**
   ```markdown
   # Integration Tests
   
   ## Prerequisites
   
   - Node.js (v16+)
   - npm
   
   ## Running
   
   ```bash
   # Run all integration tests
   just test-integration
   
   # Or directly
   cargo test --package botticelli_mcp_client \
              --features integration \
              -- --include-ignored
   ```
   
   ## Available Tests
   
   - `filesystem_integration_test` - Tests with @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem
   ```

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- ✅ Real filesystem server spawns successfully
- ✅ Tools discovered correctly
- ✅ read_file tool works end-to-end
- ✅ list_directory tool works end-to-end
- ✅ Content parsing handles all types
