## Risk Assessment

### Low Risk ✅
- Type replacements (compile-time safe)
- Deprecation strategy (backward compatible temporarily)
- Test coverage (catches regressions)
- pmcp is battle-tested (mature library)

### Medium Risk ⚠️
- Breaking API changes (mitigated by deprecation aliases)
- pmcp API changes (mitigated by version pinning)
- Content type conversions (mitigated by helpers)

### High Risk 🔴
- External server compatibility (mitigated by integration tests)
- Schema validation strictness (mitigated by good error messages)
- Downstream consumers need updates (mitigated by communication)

**Mitigation Strategies:**
- Pin pmcp version: `pmcp = "=1.8.6"`
- Comprehensive test suite before changes
- Integration tests before merging
- Phased rollout with feature flags if needed
- Clear migration guide for consumers

